Definition:
    -Dependency injection is a programming paradigm where instead of a class creating the objects it requires,
     the object is created elsewhere and then the object is just given to the class.



How to do it:
    -Its mainly done with the use-case of interfaces where there would be multiple implementations of the interface




Why dependency injection:
    -Its mainly done to avoid tight coupling of classes and encourage loosely coupled code
    -If the implementation changes then we just have to give a different object rather than do changes in the class
     which also encourages the Open-Close principles of SOLID principles
